oints, graphemes, normalization: external crates.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Code points","Graphemes","Normalization"],"captions":["Python's chars() and len() count code points: é is one char or two (e + ´)","What a person sees is a grapheme cluster; std has none, use unicode-segmentation","NFC and NFD normalization: unicode-normalization crate (unicodedata in Python)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"é — 1 point","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"e + ´ — 2 points","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":260.0,"h":40.0,"text":"👨‍👩‍👧  — 5 code points, 1 grapheme","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"unicodedata\n.normalize","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"unicode-\nnormalization","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.9,30.9]}]},{"title":"Bytes","sub":"encode and decode","short":"Bytes","main":"as_bytes, from_utf8, from_utf8_lossy; encoding_rs.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["encode / as_bytes","decode / from_utf8","lossy and encodings"],"captions":["s.encode() → s.as_bytes() (a slice, no copy) or to_vec() (a copy)","b.decode() → String::from_utf8(b): a Result — bytes may not be UTF-8","from_utf8_lossy swaps bad bytes for �; cp1251 and koi8-r: encoding_rs crate"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["s.encode()      # Python","s.as_bytes()    // &[u8]"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["String::from_utf8(bytes)","// Ok(String) or Err(…)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["String::from_utf8_lossy(&bytes)","// replaces bad bytes with �"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.8,31.7]}]},{"title":"Safety","sub":"UTF-8 boundary","short":"Safety","main":"Every String is valid UTF-8; OsString and Path.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Always UTF-8","Boundary","OsString and Path"],"captions":["Every Rust string is valid UTF-8: the type guarantees it","Decoding errors happen only at the boundary: reading a file, network, bytes","File names and paths need not be Unicode: OsString and Path, convert explicitly before printing"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":240.0,"h":40.0,"text":"String ⇒ valid UTF-8","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"bytes\nfrom outside","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"from_utf8\nResult","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"OsString","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Path","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.1,20.4]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Recap","main":"Next: lists, arrays, vectors.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["len counts bytes; no indexing; find → Option; split → iterator; format! checked at build","push_str and with_capacity instead of join; Unicode = code points; UTF-8 boundary = Result","Next chapter: Python lists, Rust arrays and vectors"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"len","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"find","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"split","tone":"gr